# drive.defaults — GLOBAL defaults for drive.sh, shared by every feature/run.
# One-time install:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/pipeline-driver && cp drive.defaults.example ~/.config/pipeline-driver/drive.defaults
# Sourced by bash BEFORE the per-feature drive.config, so anything here is a
# default and drive.config always wins. Keep per-feature facts (WORKDIR, BRANCH,
# FEATURE, the per-run ORCA_TERMINAL_HANDLE) OUT of this file.
#
# Slot bindings on this machine (documentation, not mechanism — CONTRACT.md keeps
# runtime binding out of roles.yaml on purpose; the operator assigns the bots):
#   prd / arch / task : Claude (frontier reasoning tier, e.g. opus/fable)
#   impl              : pi TUI via the orca transport (cheap coding model)
#   review            : codex (independent reviewer; merge confirm stays HUMAN)

# --- impl transport + model (stable across features) ---------------------------
# claude: spawn a headless `claude` child per card. orca: type IMPL_SLASH_CMD into a
# live Orca-managed TUI (e.g. pi) and poll the remote journal (use when the impl
# model's plan only allows interactive coding tools). herdr: same driven-TUI shape
# through a Herdr pane (`herdr pane run`; read-first {done,idle} guard; fails closed
# unless Herdr's agent detection is hook/manifest-authoritative).
IMPL_TRANSPORT=orca
IMPL_SLASH_CMD=/skill:pipeline-impl   # pi registers skills as /skill:<name>
# ORCA_RESET_CMD=/new                 # per-card TUI reset; empty = off
# ORCA_TERMINAL_TITLE=impl            # title fallback only — pin the HANDLE per run in drive.config
# HERDR_RESET_CMD=/new                # herdr: per-card TUI reset (both sides guarded); empty = off
# HERDR_PANE_CWD_MATCH=               # herdr: cwd SUBSTRING replacing the ==WORKDIR pane filter (TUI in a subdir)
# TUI_SKILLS_DIR=$HOME/.pi/agent/skills   # where the TUI agent loads skills; doctor checks the impl slot resolves THERE
# IMPL_MODEL=haiku                    # claude transport only; floor haiku, any alias or model id
# Gateway (claude transport, non-Anthropic Anthropic-compatible model, e.g. GLM):
# IMPL_AUTH_TOKEN_ENV names an EXISTING env var holding the token (never written here).
# IMPL_BASE_URL=
# IMPL_AUTH_TOKEN_ENV=

# --- loop tuning ----------------------------------------------------------------
# CARD_TIMEOUT=2700          # orca/herdr transports: max seconds to wait for one card
# POLL_SECS=30               # orca/herdr transports: journal poll interval
# ORCA_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000 # orca: wait-for-tui-idle budget before each send
# HERDR_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000 # herdr: status-guard budget before each send
# MAX_CONSEC_FAIL=2          # circuit breaker: consecutive failed impl runs
# RETRY_ON_FAIL=1            # 1 = auto-retry informed failures (attempts<3); 0 = halt each
# SETTINGS=/abs/path/to/settings.driver.json   # claude transport --settings template

# --- YOLO: standing ex-ante grant (README §YOLO) --------------------------------
# 1 = record ONCE that, for LOW-RISK features driven on this machine, the
# coordinating agent may read the frozen spec and echo the spec-rev at GATE 1 —
# no per-run chat authorization needed. This does NOT auto-start drive (starting
# ./drive.sh stays an explicit per-feature act), never delegates the merge
# confirm, and DANGEROUS features (external write-paths) never use the driver.
YOLO=0

# --- sibling repos (drive.sh doctor, board rendering) ------------------------------
# PIPELINE_REPO=$HOME/workspace/pipeline
# DASHBOARD_REPO=$HOME/workspace/pipeline-dashboard
# SKILLS_DIR=$HOME/.agents/skills

# --- board auto-refresh -------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-empty = re-render the read-only dashboard here after GATE 1, after every
# advanced card, and on halt (needs node + a built DASHBOARD_REPO). Open it in a
# browser and refresh whenever you glance over.
# BOARD_OUT=/tmp/pipeline-board.html

# --- review-drive.sh: the meta-PR review<->fix loop (README §review-drive) ----------
# Drives ONE toolchain-repo PR between the reviewer TUI (REVIEW_TERMINAL_* below)
# and a fixer TUI until 'verdict: approved', a cap, or a no-progress halt. The
# merge stays yours. Pin FIX_TERMINAL_HANDLE per run in review-drive.config —
# only stable tuning belongs here.
# FIX_TERMINAL_TITLE=pi        # title fallback only — pin the HANDLE per run
# REVIEW_REPO=jackypanster/pipeline   # repo for bare-number PR arguments
# REVIEW_REPO_RE='^jackypanster/pipeline(-driver|-dashboard|-dispatch)?$'  # ENFORCED scope
# PROTOCOL_AUTHOR=             # protocol-comment identity; default: the gh-authenticated login
# REVIEW_SLASH_CMD is shared with the one-key relay (below) and REQUIRED non-empty by
# review-drive (default /pipeline-review): the relayed review must BE pipeline-review.
# MAX_ROUNDS=5                 # hard cap on review rounds (PR #39 took 8 WITH a human curating)
# HUNT_AFTER=3                 # fix dispatch >= this switches to the root-cause template
# REVIEW_TIMEOUT=2700          # max seconds to wait for one verdict comment
# FIX_TIMEOUT=2700             # max seconds to wait for one pushed fix + evidence

# --- one-key review relay (README §Board & review relay) ----------------------------
# When the loop halts at NEXT=review, OFFER to type "$REVIEW_SLASH_CMD repo=… branch=…"
# into the review terminal (e.g. codex) — you read the halt, you press y. Never
# automatic; GATE 2 (semantic review + HUMAN merge confirm) is untouched.
# Pin the HANDLE per run (orca terminal list --json; handles die on app restart), or
# give a unique title substring for discovery.
# REVIEW_TERMINAL_HANDLE=term_...
# REVIEW_TERMINAL_TITLE=codex
# REVIEW_SLASH_CMD='$pipeline-review'   # codex >=0.144 invokes skills with a $-prefix from
#                                       # ~/.codex/skills — SINGLE-QUOTE the value (unquoted,
#                                       # bash would expand $pipeline to empty). /pipeline-review
#                                       # is the claude-style default.
